Thanks for the review! I've pushed fixes for all three and replied on each.

For the type diff, I ran openapi-typescript 7.13.0 with `--root-types` (what gemara-react pins) on the `openapi.yaml` from main and from this branch. This is all that changes in the three types:

```diff
 AssessmentLog: {
     ...
-};
+} & ({
+    /** @enum {string} */
+    result?: "Not Run" | "Unknown" | "Not Applicable";
+} | unknown);

 Mapping: {
     ...
-};
+} & ({
+    /** @enum {string} */
+    relationship?: "no-match";
+} | unknown);

 Evidence: {
     ...
-};
+} & (unknown | unknown);
```

The other branch of each `anyOf` is a bare `required`, which openapi-typescript turns into `unknown`. That makes each union `unknown`, and `T & unknown` is just `T`. I checked it with `tsc`: every type in `components["schemas"]` comes out identical between the two files, these three included. So gemara-react's types don't change. The rule can't be written as a TS type, so it only shows up in the hover docs: the AssessmentLog and Mapping descriptions now include the rule sentence, and the start rule no longer appears in the "enforced by the CUE schema" note on `assessment-logs`.
